IMPORT prelude

-- Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank Act 2015 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a person or business dealing with the Bank:
-- when the Bank can be sued and where (Schedule, Article 46(1), (2)), when its property can be seized or taken (Articles 46(3),
-- 47(1)), the immunity of its officers, employees, experts and consultants (Article 50(i)), the Bank's tax and customs exemption and
-- the limits s 7(2) puts on it (Article 51(1)), tax on Bank pay (Article 51(2)), tax on securities the Bank issues or guarantees
-- (Article 51(3), (4)), waiver (Article 52), and the Minister's subscription limits (s 4).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/AIIBA2015.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". Its legislative history lists only
-- Act 24 of 2015 (commenced 22 August 2015) and the 2017 Revised Edition (Chapter 15A); no amending Act is annotated. The arrangement
-- of sections at the top of the deposit is one line out of step with the body; the body's numbering (ss 1-9) is followed here.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0157 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. SCOPED to the provisions a claimant, contractor, employee, bondholder or taxpayer would meet. Not encoded:
-- the deposit of the instrument of ratification (s 3), the Consolidated Fund provisions (ss 5, 6), the Minister's power to amend the
-- Schedule (s 7(3)), s 8 (the Companies Act 1967 does not apply to the Bank or its securities -- stated in NOTES only), regulations
-- (s 9), juridical personality (Article 45), archives (Article 47(2)), freedom from restrictions (Article 48), communications
-- (Article 49), and immigration, exchange and travel treatment of staff (Article 50(ii), (iii)).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank Act 2015 -- immunities and exemptions`

§§ `Schedule, Article 46(1), (2) and Article 52 -- suing the Bank`

-- Article 46(1): "The Bank shall enjoy immunity from every form of legal process, except in cases arising out of or in connection
-- with the exercise of its powers to raise funds, through borrowings or other means, to guarantee obligations, or to buy and sell or
-- underwrite the sale of securities, in which cases actions may be brought against the Bank only in a court of competent jurisdiction
-- in the territory of a country in which the Bank has an office, or has appointed an agent for the purpose of accepting service or
-- notice of process, or has issued or guaranteed securities."
-- Article 46(2): "no action shall be brought against the Bank by any member, or by any agency or instrumentality of a member, or by
-- any entity or person directly or indirectly acting for or deriving claims from a member".
-- Article 52(1): the Bank "at its discretion may waive any of the privileges, immunities and exemptions conferred under this Chapter
-- in any case or instance".
-- s 7(1): "Despite anything to the contrary in any other law", the Schedule has the force of law.
--
-- INFERENCE: a waiver is treated as lifting both the para 1 immunity (and with it the forum condition, which attaches only to the
-- excepted cases) and the para 2 bar. The text does not say whether para 2 is an "immunity" capable of waiver.

DECLARE Claim IS ONE OF
    `a holder suing on a bond the Bank issued`
    `a lender suing on money the Bank borrowed`
    `a creditor suing on a guarantee the Bank gave`
    `a dealer suing over the Bank's purchase or sale of securities`
    `an underwriter suing over an underwriting by the Bank`
    `an employee suing over employment`
    `a supplier suing on an unpaid invoice`
    `a visitor suing for personal injury on Bank premises`
    `a person suing for defamation`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim arises from fund-raising, guarantees or securities dealing` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `a holder suing on a bond the Bank issued` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a lender suing on money the Bank borrowed` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a creditor suing on a guarantee the Bank gave` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a dealer suing over the Bank's purchase or sale of securities` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an underwriter suing over an underwriting by the Bank` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim,
      `the claimant is a member or acts for or derives its claim from a member` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Bank has an office, an agent for service, or issued or guaranteed securities in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Bank has waived its immunity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an action may be brought against the Bank in a Singapore court` IF
        ((NOT `the claimant is a member or acts for or derives its claim from a member`) OR `the Bank has waived its immunity`)
    AND (    `the Bank has waived its immunity`
         OR (    `the claim arises from fund-raising, guarantees or securities dealing` `the claim`
             AND `the Bank has an office, an agent for service, or issued or guaranteed securities in Singapore`))

§§ `Schedule, Articles 46(3) and 47(1) -- seizing or taking the Bank's property`

-- Article 46(3): property and assets of the Bank "shall, wheresoever located and by whomsoever held, be immune from all forms of
-- seizure, attachment or execution before the delivery of final judgment against the Bank".
-- Article 47(1): property and assets of the Bank "shall be immune from search, requisition, confiscation, expropriation or any other
-- form of taking or foreclosure by executive or legislative action".
--
-- INFERENCE: after final judgment, Article 46(3) no longer bars judicial execution, and Article 47(1) reaches only executive or
-- legislative action, so neither bars execution of a final judgment. The text does not say so in terms.

GIVEN `final judgment has been delivered against the Bank` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the taking is by executive or legislative action` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Bank has waived the immunity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seizure or taking of Bank property is barred` IF
        (NOT `the Bank has waived the immunity`)
    AND (`the taking is by executive or legislative action` OR (NOT `final judgment has been delivered against the Bank`))

§§ `Schedule, Article 50(i) -- officers, employees, experts and consultants`

-- Article 50: "All Governors, Directors, Alternates, the President, Vice-Presidents and other officers and employees of the Bank,
-- including experts and consultants performing missions or services for the Bank: (i) shall be immune from legal process with respect
-- to acts performed by them in their official capacity, except when the Bank waives the immunity".

GIVEN `the person is a Governor, Director, Alternate, officer, employee, expert or consultant of the Bank` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the act was performed in an official capacity` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Bank has waived the person's immunity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is immune from legal process for the act` IF
        `the person is a Governor, Director, Alternate, officer, employee, expert or consultant of the Bank`
    AND `the act was performed in an official capacity`
    AND (NOT `the Bank has waived the person's immunity`)

§§ `Schedule, Article 51(1) and s 7(2) -- the Bank's own taxes and duties`

-- Article 51(1): "The Bank, its assets, property, income and its operations and transactions pursuant to this Agreement, shall be
-- exempt from all taxation and from all customs duties. The Bank shall also be exempt from any obligation for the payment,
-- withholding or collection of any tax or duty."
-- s 7(2): nothing in Article 51 is to be construed as "(a) entitling the Bank to import into Singapore goods free of any customs duty
-- without any restriction on their subsequent sale in Singapore; (b) conferring on the Bank any exemption from taxes or duties that
-- form part of the price of goods sold or services supplied; or (c) conferring on the Bank any exemption from taxes or duties that are
-- in fact no more than charges for services rendered."
--
-- INFERENCE for (a): goods imported subject to a restriction on resale in Singapore remain within the customs exemption; s 7(2)(a)
-- withholds only duty-free import with no restriction on resale.

DECLARE Charge IS ONE OF
    `income tax on the Bank's income`
    `property tax on the Bank's property`
    `stamp duty on a Bank transaction`
    `customs duty on goods imported subject to a restriction on resale in Singapore`
    `customs duty on goods imported with no restriction on resale in Singapore`
    `tax forming part of the price of goods or services the Bank buys`
    `a charge that is in fact no more than a charge for services rendered`
    `a duty to withhold or collect tax on payments the Bank makes`

GIVEN `the charge` IS A Charge
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Bank is exempt from the charge` IF
    CONSIDER `the charge`
    WHEN `customs duty on goods imported with no restriction on resale in Singapore` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `tax forming part of the price of goods or services the Bank buys` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a charge that is in fact no more than a charge for services rendered` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Schedule, Article 51(2) -- tax on pay from the Bank`

-- Article 51(2): "No tax of any kind shall be levied on or in respect of salaries, emoluments and expenses, as the case may be, paid by
-- the Bank to Directors, Alternate Directors, the President, Vice-Presidents and other officers or employees of the Bank, including
-- experts and consultants performing missions or services for the Bank, except where a member deposits with its instrument of
-- ratification, acceptance, or approval a declaration that such member retains for itself and its political subdivisions the right to
-- tax salaries, and emoluments, as the case may be, paid by the Bank to citizens or nationals of such member."
--
-- The retained right covers "salaries, and emoluments"; "expenses" are not in it. Whether Singapore deposited such a declaration is
-- NOT in the deposit (s 3 describes the instrument of ratification without mentioning one), so it is an input.

GIVEN `paid by the Bank to a Director, officer, employee, expert or consultant` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the payment is expenses rather than salary or emoluments` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the recipient is a Singapore citizen or national` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `Singapore deposited a declaration retaining the right to tax` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Singapore may tax the payment` IF
        (NOT `paid by the Bank to a Director, officer, employee, expert or consultant`)
    OR (    `Singapore deposited a declaration retaining the right to tax`
        AND `the recipient is a Singapore citizen or national`
        AND (NOT `the payment is expenses rather than salary or emoluments`))

§§ `Schedule, Article 51(3), (4) -- tax on securities the Bank issues or guarantees`

-- Article 51(3): no tax "on any obligation or security issued by the Bank, including any dividend or interest thereon, by whomsoever
-- held: (i) which discriminates against such obligation or security solely because it is issued by the Bank; or (ii) if the sole
-- jurisdictional basis for such taxation is the place or currency in which it is issued, made payable or paid, or the location of any
-- office or place of business maintained by the Bank."
-- Article 51(4): the same for a security "guaranteed by the Bank", but (ii) names only "the location of any office or place of
-- business maintained by the Bank" -- not the place or currency of issue or payment.
-- The basis given below is taken to be the SOLE jurisdictional basis for the tax.

DECLARE Basis IS ONE OF
    `the holder's residence or business in Singapore`
    `the place where the security is issued, made payable or paid`
    `the currency in which the security is issued, made payable or paid`
    `the location of a Bank office or place of business`

GIVEN `the Bank issued the security rather than guaranteed it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the tax discriminates solely because of the Bank's issue or guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the sole basis` IS A Basis
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tax on the security is barred` IF
        `the tax discriminates solely because of the Bank's issue or guarantee`
    OR  CONSIDER `the sole basis`
        WHEN `the location of a Bank office or place of business` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the place where the security is issued, made payable or paid` THEN `the Bank issued the security rather than guaranteed it`
        WHEN `the currency in which the security is issued, made payable or paid` THEN `the Bank issued the security rather than guaranteed it`
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `4 -- the Minister's subscription limits`

-- s 4(1)(a): the Minister may subscribe to shares of the original authorised capital stock "to an amount not exceeding US$250
-- million"; (b), (c) increases under Article 5(3), (4). s 4(2): "The total subscription to the Bank may not exceed the sum of US$500
-- million unless increased with the approval of Parliament signified by resolution." Amounts below are in US$ millions.

GIVEN `original capital stock subscribed` IS A NUMBER,
      `total subscribed` IS A NUMBER,
      `Parliament has approved a higher total by resolution` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the total Parliament approved` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the subscription is within the Minister's power` IF
        `original capital stock subscribed` AT MOST 250
    AND (    `total subscribed` AT MOST 500
         OR (`Parliament has approved a higher total by resolution` AND `total subscribed` AT MOST `the total Parliament approved`))
